# What the deploy must NOT serve.
#
# Vercel has no build step here, so every file in the deployed directory is
# fetchable at its path. Repo visibility is irrelevant to that: a private repo
# still serves a public site. So anything sensitive has to be excluded here, not
# hidden on GitHub.
#
# The live exposure this closes: prompts/profile.md states her F-1 status and
# visa timing, a $2.5M book of business, and a candid note that her depth under
# technical questioning is thinner than her communication. The resume PDF carries
# her mobile number. All of it was readable at a guessable URL.
prompts/
resume/
tests/
ingest/
schema/

# Docs. Nothing on the site links them and they describe the internals.
CLAUDE.md
CONTRACT.md
SOURCES.md
designprompt.md
package.json

# NOT ignored, because the board fetches them at runtime:
#   index.html, styles.css, app.js
#   data/sample-opportunities.json, data/sample-digest.json   (Load sample data)
#   data/digests/                                             (auto-import)
#
# README.md is left served on purpose: it is the project's public face and
# contains nothing about her that she has not chosen to publish.
